cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ESAC in research, evaluation reports, or comparative claims, cite this repository and always state the suite version you measured against."
title: "ESAC: EcoWestern Short and Cheap Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  A program of compact benchmarks that measure difficult capabilities without measuring
  budget. ESAC-GI (General Intelligence) is released; ESAC-AG (Agentic Work and Capability)
  is specified and not implemented. Items are generators rather than stored questions, so
  expected answers are computed rather than recalled, and every score is reported against a
  version tag that names the instrument which produced it.
type: software
authors:
  - name: EcoWestern
    website: "https://github.com/EcoWestern"
repository-code: "https://github.com/EcoWestern/ESAC"
url: "https://ecowestern.github.io/ESAC/"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/EcoWestern/ESAC/blob/main/LICENSE"
date-released: "2026-09-22"
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - evaluation
  - large language models
  - general intelligence
  - agentic evaluation
  - reproducibility
  - contamination resistance
